{"_id":"68a736318ec3d8323af1cc65","nodeId":"zOENl96GUZRw2PP2KxIck","roadmapSlug":"react","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:28.899Z","description":"# High Order Components\n\nA higher-order component (HOC) is an advanced technique in React for reusing component logic. HOCs are not part of the React API, per se. They are a pattern that emerges from ReactΓÇÖs compositional nature.\n\nConcretely, a higher-order component is a function that takes a component and returns a new component.\n\nHigher-order components are not commonly used in modern React code. In order to reuse logic, React hooks are mainly used now.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"High-Order Components","url":"https://reactjs.org/docs/higher-order-components.html","_id":"6a7f4f9dcb44947debd1c170"},{"type":"article","title":"How to create a Higher-Order Component","url":"https://www.robinwieruch.de/react-higher-order-components/","_id":"6a7f4f9dcb44947debd1c171"},{"type":"video","title":"Learn React Higher Order Component (HOC) in 10 Minutes","url":"https://youtu.be/J5P0q7EROfw?si=-8s5h1b0mZSGVgLt","_id":"6a7f4f9dcb44947debd1c172"},{"type":"video","title":"ReactJS Tutorial - Higher Order Components (Part 1)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B6aNv8nkUSw","_id":"6a7f4f9dcb44947debd1c173"},{"type":"video","title":"ReactJS Tutorial - Higher Order Components (Part 2)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rsBQj6X7UK8","_id":"6a7f4f9dcb44947debd1c174"},{"type":"video","title":"ReactJS Tutorial - Higher Order Components (Part 3)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l8V59zIdBXU","_id":"6a7f4f9dcb44947debd1c175"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:25:49.234Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dbfb5fcb94d04163ae","title":"Scrimba - Advanced React","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"https://v2.scrimba.com/advanced-react-c02h?via=roadmap"},{"_id":"6a5e04dbfb5fcb94d04163fe","title":"Scrimba - Build a Movie Search App in React","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"https://v2.scrimba.com